{"schemaVersion": "bedrock-conversation-2024", "system": [{"text": "You are a helpful conversational assistant. Engage in natural, friendly dialogue."}], "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": [{"text": "It ’ s an article about language . It talks about the idea of having a single global language ."}]}, {"role": "assistant", "content": [{"text": "It seems that English already is the main global language . Does the article suggest that there should be an artificial language like Esperanto as the world language ."}]}, {"role": "user", "content": [{"text": "Actually , it suggest English . The main argument is that English is already being studied as a second language in most countries-china , India , mexico , Nigeria , Pakistan , and japan . So beginning again with a language like Esperanto would be wasteful . The second argument is that English is used in modern technology far more that any other language . Most emails are sent in English and the vast majority of website use English ."}]}, {"role": "assistant", "content": [{"text": "Does the article say anything about other language ? How will they survive in an English-speaking world ?"}]}, {"role": "user", "content": [{"text": "The article points out that many languages have been lost and will be lost , but others will continue to be used for generation , even if English continues to be the dominant language ."}]}, {"role": "assistant", "content": [{"text": "Right . All the people who speak Chinese . Hindi , French and Spanish aren ’ t suddenly going to stop using those languages .\nIn that case , I shall continue to learning a few basic phrases in other languages ."}]}]}
